            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Management of angina pectoris begins with recognition of the disorder and with an assessment of the extent and severity of the underlying disorder. Management includes adjunctive measures, antianginal drug therapy, and mechanical (surgery, angioplasty) options.</AbstractText>
